accessWidener	v2	named

# NOTE: the header above MUST be the first line — AccessWidenerReader rejects the file
# outright if a comment precedes it ("Invalid access widener file header").
#
# The remediation for the reflection sites tracked by scripts/check_remap_safety.py.
#
# `named` = the Mojang names this repo compiles against (build.gradle:63
# `mappings loom.officialMojangMappings()`). Loom remaps THIS FILE to whatever
# namespace each artifact ships in, which is the whole point: the member reference in
# the source becomes an ordinary field/method access that tiny-remapper rewrites like
# any other, instead of a string constant it leaves alone.
#
# Every member here replaced a reflective lookup that broke in the remapped fabric jar.
# Descriptors are in the NAMED namespace: tiny v2's descriptor column is OFFICIAL, so an
# object type must be translated (causeOfDeath is `Lwz;` there, not `LComponent;`).
#
# Why these two cannot be fixed any other way: ClientInput WRITES them
# (`fx.setDouble(mh, wx)`), and vanilla exposes only a getter (`xpos()`), so there is
# no public API to call. On Xvfb `glfwSetCursorPos` does not fire the cursor_pos
# callback, so without this write MouseHandler keeps stale coordinates and tooltips
# render at the previous hover spot.

accessible	field	net/minecraft/client/MouseHandler	xpos	D
accessible	field	net/minecraft/client/MouseHandler	ypos	D

